              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ねだる (nedaru) is a native Japanese word (wago), inherited rather than borrowed from Chinese. JMdict marks it as usually written in kana; its kanji spelling borrows characters meaning \"strong\" and \"ask\", chosen for the meaning and not the sound (JMdict, KANJIDIC2)."
